            from: [
                "test('a generator handler streams, and the value is its chunks'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/url.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a record or a list of records rides the query as its canonical JSON — 30.28'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/diffOps.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a keyed list is changed row by row, and the ops rebuild it — 18.41'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/durableFollow.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a restart over the same store keeps the version, and the patches since — 18.42, 18.43'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/wireCopy.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a copy given a debounce sends one request for the keys a page reaches inside the window",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/appAddresses.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('rpc.tool is the name MCP lists the handler by, under a mount too",
            ],
        },

        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/rpc.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a mutation runs again on a later call, where a read serves what it holds — 16.7'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/refreshes.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a call that answers refreshes its tags, and one refused refreshes nothing — 16.89'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/rpcMethods.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('an rpc answers the verbs its value does, or the ones methods names — 16.111, 16.112'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/rpcMethods.test.ts',
            from: [
                'test("a value\'s PUT writes it and its PATCH patches it where methods names them, each answering the value — 16.111, 16.115"',
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/rpcMethods.test.ts',
            from: [
                'test("a browser\'s set and patch of a value are sent as PUT and PATCH — 16.116"',
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/rpcMethods.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a GET whose args outgrow its URL is sent as QUERY and answered as the GET — 16.114'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/appAddresses.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a server file answers its default at its route, each named rpc below it, and an address where it says — 16.2, 16.113'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Read one deal by its id">
        <p>Write the read in a handler file. The parameter's annotation is its <code>Args</code>,
            checked on every call, and <code>description</code> is the sentence every surface
            shows.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { refuse } from '@abide/abide'
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { DEALS } from '../pipeline/lib/DEALS.server.ts'

            export default rpc(
                ({ id }: { id: string }) =>
                    DEALS.find((deal) => deal.id === id) ?? refuse(404),
                { description: 'One deal, by id.' },
            )
        `} />
        <p>That file answers at its path. Here is the CRM's, asked over HTTP when this page
            loaded:</p>
        <Exchange path="/deals/getDeal?id=d1" />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Show the deal a page picks">
        <p>Import the handler file and call it inside a <code>reactive</code>. The call answers a
            promise, and the <code>reactive</code> makes it live: the page reads
            <code>deal.name</code> by name and loads again when <code>id</code> changes.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { reactive } from '@abide/abide'
            import getDeal from './getDeal.server.ts'

            let id = reactive('d1')
            const deal = reactive(() => getDeal({ id }))
            </script>

            <button onclick={() => (id = 'd2')}>Next deal</button>
            <h2>{deal.name}</h2>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Send the activity archive an entry at a time">
        <p>Write the handler as an async generator and it streams. A <code>reactive</code>
            reading it holds every entry that has arrived, and its <code>busy()</code> stays true
            until the stream closes.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'

            const OLDER = [
                { on: '2026-09-02', note: 'Intro call, asked for pricing' },
                { on: '2026-09-09', note: 'Sent the proposal' },
                { on: '2026-10-01', note: 'Signed for 40 seats' },
            ]

            export default rpc(async function* () {
                for (const entry of OLDER) {
                    await Bun.sleep(600) // a slow archive
                    yield entry
                }
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Link to the deals export as a download">
        <p>A link cannot call a handler, so give it <code>url()</code>: the address from the
            file's path and the mount. A handler returning a <code>Blob</code> answers with the
            blob's own type.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import exportDeals from './exportDeals.server.ts'
            </script>

            <a href={exportDeals.url()} download="deals.csv">Download deals</a>
        `} />
        <p>The CRM's export, and the CRM's answer:</p>
        <Exchange path="/deals/exportDeals" />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Filter the deals by a record">
        <p>Give an arg a record, or a list of records, and it rides the URL as JSON with its keys
            sorted, so one filter is one address. A list of plain values repeats its name. The
            handler reads both back as its <code>Args</code> declares them.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`
            import searchDeals from './searchDeals.server.ts'

            const address = searchDeals.url({
                filter: { stage: 'won', owner: 'ada' },
                ids: [1, 2],
            })
            decodeURIComponent(address)
            // /deals/searchDeals?filter={"owner":"ada","stage":"won"}&ids=1&ids=2
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Spot the assistant drafting a report as it streams">
        <p><code>tool</code> is the name MCP lists the handler by, the name a model's
            <code>tool_use</code> carries. It is read off the route, so it stays the same under a
            sub-path.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`
            import draftReport from './draftReport.server.ts'

            // 'post_ops_draftReport'
            const drafting = (block: { type: string; name?: string }) =>
                block.type === 'tool_use' && block.name === draftReport.tool
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Reload only the pipeline stages a win changed">
        <p>Pass the handler's <code>refresh</code> a pattern of its args, and the entries matching
            it load again while every other stage stays as it is.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`
            import getStage from './getStage.server.ts'
            import winDeal from './winDeal.server.ts'

            await winDeal()
            getStage.refresh({ stage: 'lead' })
            getStage.refresh({ stage: 'won' })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Send every tab the call just logged, and nothing else">
        <p>Make the read <code>global</code> and write it on the server with
            <code>patch</code>. Every page reading it follows it, and a change reaches each one as
            the JSON Patch from the value it replaced, so a logged call is one row on the wire
            rather than the list again. <code>key</code> says which row is which.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import listCalls, { type Call } from './listCalls.server.ts'

            export default rpc(({ id, note }: Call) => {
                listCalls.patch((held) => {
                    if (!held.some((call) => call.id === id)) held.push({ id, note })
                })
            }, { methods: ['POST'] })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Search the deals once the typing stops">
        <p>Give the read a <code>debounce</code>, and every page calling it is held to it: the first
            query is searched at once, and one typed after it once the typing pauses rather than
            once per keystroke. The page reads the handler as it would any other.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { DEALS } from './lib/DEALS.server.ts'

            export default rpc(
                ({ q }: { q: string }) => {
                    const names: string[] = []
                    for (const deal of DEALS)
                        if (deal.name.toLowerCase().includes(q.toLowerCase()))
                            names.push(deal.name)
                    return names
                },
                { debounce: 300 },
            )
        `} />
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { reactive } from '@abide/abide'
            import searchDeals from '../searchDeals.server.ts'

            let q = reactive('')
            const found = reactive(() => searchDeals({ q }))
            </script>

            <input bind:value={q}>
            {#for name of found}<p>{name}</p>{/for}
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Keep the call log's versions across a restart">
        <p>Give the read a <code>store</code> that keeps a log, <code>store.sqlite</code> or
            <code>store.redis</code>, and each change is a numbered record in it. A restarted
            server stands at the same version, so a page that reconnects is sent only the patches
            it missed. A second server on the same store applies the first one's records and sends
            them to its own followers.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { rpc, store } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { crmDatabase } from '../pipeline/lib/crmDatabase.server.ts'

            export type Call = { id: string; note: string }

            export default rpc((): Call[] => [], {
                global: true,
                key: 'id',
                store: store.sqlite<Call[]>(crmDatabase, 'calls'),
            })
        `} />
    </Section>
    <Section level={3} title="Move a deal to another stage">
        <p>Declare a write by naming its verb in <code>methods</code> — <code>POST</code>,
            <code>PUT</code>, <code>PATCH</code> or <code>DELETE</code>. It takes what a read
            takes, and the page never names the method.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { refuse } from '@abide/abide'
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { DEALS } from '../pipeline/lib/DEALS.server.ts'

            export default rpc(
                ({ id, stage }: { id: string; stage: string }) => {
                    const deal = DEALS.find((each) => each.id === id)
                    if (deal === undefined) return refuse(404)
                    deal.stage = stage
                    return { ...deal }
                },
                { methods: ['PATCH'], description: 'Moves a deal to another stage.' },
            )
        `} />
        <p>Ask the CRM's address with another method and it answers 405, with the one it takes
            in <code>allow</code>:</p>
        <Exchange path="/deals/moveDeal" />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Run the write again on every click">
        <p>A mutation keeps nothing, so each call runs the handler. Await the call for its answer,
            or catch its refusal.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { reactive } from '@abide/abide'
            import moveDeal from './moveDeal.server.ts'

            let stage = reactive('proposal')
            async function win() {
                stage = (await moveDeal({ id: 'd2', stage: 'won' })).stage
            }
            </script>

            <button onclick={win}>Mark won</button> {stage}
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Reload every tab showing the stages a write changed">
        <p>List the tags the write changes in <code>refreshes</code>. Before the write answers,
            the server reloads the entries carrying them, in every tab following them.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { DEALS } from './lib/DEALS.server.ts'

            export default rpc(
                () => {
                    const deal = DEALS.find((each) => each.stage === 'lead')
                    if (deal) deal.stage = 'qualified'
                    return deal?.id ?? null
                },
                { methods: ['POST'], refreshes: ['stage:lead', 'stage:qualified'] },
            )
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Log a call with no network">
        <p>Give the call <code>offline</code>. Where the network fails, the call settles to what
            it returns and the write waits in <code>outbox</code> to be sent.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`
            import listCalls from './listCalls.server.ts'
            import logCall from './logCall.server.ts'

            const call = { id: crypto.randomUUID(), note: 'Wants a demo' }
            logCall(call, {
                offline: () => listCalls.patch((held) => held.push(call)),
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Keep the team's seat count, written from any page">
        <p>Hand <code>rpc</code> a value, and it answers <code>GET</code> with it. Name
            <code>PUT</code> and <code>PATCH</code> in <code>methods</code> to change it from a
            page. It is the server's one value: a page's <code>set</code> or <code>patch</code>
            shows at once, is sent, and the copy then holds what the server answered.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'

            export default rpc(
                { seats: 40 },
                {
                    methods: ['GET', 'PUT', 'PATCH'],
                    description: 'The seats the team holds.',
                },
            )
        `} />
        <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`
            import seats from './seats.server.ts'

            seats.patch((held) => {
                held.seats += 1
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Answer the pipeline's reads from one server file">
        <p>Export as many as the file needs. The default answers at the file's route, each named
            one below it by its name, and anything else it exports stays on the server.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { DEALS } from './lib/DEALS.server.ts'

            export default rpc(() => DEALS)
            export const stages = rpc(() => ['lead', 'won'])
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Publish the deals at an API path of their own">
        <p>Give it an <code>address</code>, and it answers there in place of its file's route.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { DEALS } from './lib/DEALS.server.ts'

            export const v1 = rpc(() => DEALS, { address: '/api/v1/deals' })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Search the deals by a filter too long for a link">
        <p>Call it as before. A call whose args would make its link longer than 2048 characters is
            sent as a <code>QUERY</code>, its args in the body, and answered as the read it is.</p>
    </Section>
</Doc>
